From 803fc2d6020a2372ccd647fa0eb237561ae57372 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:50:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] check: format TEST_DEV up front when RECREATE_TEST_DEV is set

RECREATE_TEST_DEV recreates the test filesystem for every section, but
check mounts TEST_DEV from init_rc at startup, before the first section
runs. A fresh, never-formatted test device therefore fails that mount and
check exits before it would have recreated the device, so the device
cannot be brought up on its first run without formatting it out of band
first.

Since the device is going to be remade anyway when RECREATE_TEST_DEV is
set, make it once up front, right after the config is sourced and before
init_rc. init_rc then mounts the freshly made filesystem and each section
still recreates it as before. This lets RECREATE_TEST_DEV initialise a raw
test device on the very first run.

Generated-by: Claude AI
Signed-off-by: Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>
---
 check | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/check b/check
index ad685edc..484d2341 100755
--- a/check
+++ b/check
@@ -362,6 +362,14 @@ if ! . ./common/rc; then
 	_fatal "check: failed to source common/rc"
 fi
 
+# When RECREATE_TEST_DEV is set the test device is remade for the first section
+# anyway; make it now so a fresh, never-formatted TEST_DEV can be mounted by
+# init_rc below on the first run instead of failing that mount.
+if $RECREATE_TEST_DEV; then
+	_test_unmount 2>/dev/null
+	_test_mkfs >/dev/null
+fi
+
 init_rc
 
 # If the test config specified a soak test duration, see if there are any
